IMPORT prelude

-- Merchant Shipping (Civil Liability and Compensation for Oil Pollution) Act 1998 (Singapore) -- which ships the owner's strict
-- liability attaches to (ss 3(3), (4), 18(1)), the owner's defences (s 4), who else is shielded from claims (s 5(1)(d), (2)), what
-- environmental loss is recoverable (s 5(3)), the owner's limit in special drawing rights and when it is lost (s 6), the time bar
-- (s 12), the compulsory insurance certificate (ss 13, 18(2)) and who may issue it (s 13(3)), the insurer as defendant (s 15(3)),
-- contributions to the International Fund (s 25(5), (6)), when the Fund pays (s 27(1), (6), (7), (9)), the Fund's cap and pro-rata
-- sharing (s 28(1), (2)), the Fund time bar (s 30), and selected offences (ss 13(6), (7), 20(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation,
-- version in force from 1/4/2022, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MSCLCOPA1998.txt. The latest amendment annotated is
-- Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022 (ss 18(4), 28(4), 29(5)). The limits in ss 6(2) and 28(1) are annotated [S 486/2003].
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. REQ-0106 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life relevance.
-- The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- SCOPED to what a shipowner, charterer, insurer, oil importer or pollution claimant meets. Not encoded: the conversion of SDRs to
-- Singapore dollars (ss 7(3), 28(5)), limitation-action procedure (ss 7(2) beyond pro-rata, 7(4) to (8), 8 to 10), jurisdiction and
-- foreign judgments (ss 16, 17, 29), the Fund's legal capacity (s 24), contribution amounts and security (s 25(7) to (11)), the
-- Director's powers (ss 14, 20(1), 21, 22, 26(1) to (4), 33, 34), joint liability of two ships (s 3(6)), the Contributory Negligence
-- link (ss 3(8), 27(8)), state-ship procedure (s 18(3), (4)), regulations, composition and body-corporate liability (ss 32, 36 to 39).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Oil pollution -- ships`

-- s 2(1): "ship" means "any sea-going vessel and seaborne craft of any type"; "oil" means "any persistent hydrocarbon mineral oil
-- such as crude oil, fuel oil, heavy diesel oil and lubricating oil, whether carried on board a ship as cargo or in the bunkers".
DECLARE Ship HAS
    `built or adapted to carry oil in bulk as cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `able to carry other cargoes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carrying oil in bulk as cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on a voyage after carrying oil in bulk` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved free of oil residues` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a warship or government non-commercial ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gross tonnage` IS A NUMBER
    `tons of oil carried in bulk as cargo` IS A NUMBER

§§ `3(3), (4) and 18(1) -- ships the owner's liability attaches to`

-- s 3(3): "this section applies to any ship constructed or adapted for carrying oil in bulk as cargo." (4): where such a ship "is
-- capable of carrying any other cargoes besides oil, this section applies only ... (a) while it is carrying oil in bulk as cargo; and
-- (b) while it is on any voyage following the carriage of any such oil, unless it is proved that no residues ... remain in the ship."
-- s 18(1): Part 2 "does not apply in relation to any warship or any ship for the time being used by the government of any State
-- otherwise than for commercial purposes."
--
-- A dedicated tanker is covered even when empty. A ship not built or adapted to carry oil cargo is outside s 3 even though "oil"
-- includes bunker fuel: the bunkers matter only for a tanker (s 2(3)(c)).
GIVEN `the ship` IS A Ship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 applies to the ship` IF
        (NOT `the ship`'s `a warship or government non-commercial ship`)
    AND `the ship`'s `built or adapted to carry oil in bulk as cargo`
    AND (    (NOT `the ship`'s `able to carry other cargoes`)
         OR  `the ship`'s `carrying oil in bulk as cargo`
         OR  (`the ship`'s `on a voyage after carrying oil in bulk` AND (NOT `the ship`'s `proved free of oil residues`))
        )

§§ `4 -- the owner's defences`

-- s 4: no liability "if the owner proves that the discharge or escape ... (a) resulted from an act of war, hostilities, civil war,
-- insurrection or an exceptional, inevitable and irresistible natural phenomenon; (b) was due WHOLLY to anything done or left undone
-- by another person, not being an employee or agent of the owner, with intent to do damage; or (c) was due WHOLLY to the negligence or
-- wrongful act of a government or other authority in exercising its functions of maintaining lights or other navigational aids".
-- s 3(1): otherwise the owner "shall ... be liable" -- no fault need be shown (s 3(8) treats the damage as if due to the owner's fault
-- for contributory negligence purposes).
DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
    `the crew's negligent navigation`
    `an act of war`
    `an exceptional, inevitable and irresistible natural phenomenon`
    `an ordinary storm`
    `sabotage wholly by an outsider`
    `sabotage by the owner's own employee`
    `sabotage by an outsider combined with crew negligence`
    `a navigational light the authority wholly failed to maintain`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner has a section 4 defence` IF
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `an act of war` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an exceptional, inevitable and irresistible natural phenomenon` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sabotage wholly by an outsider` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a navigational light the authority wholly failed to maintain` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the ship` IS A Ship, `the cause` IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is liable under section 3` IF
    `section 3 applies to the ship` `the ship` AND (NOT `the owner has a section 4 defence` `the cause`)

§§ `5(1)(d) and (2) -- persons shielded from pollution claims`

-- s 5(1): whether or not the owner is liable under s 3, "(c) the owner shall not be liable otherwise than under that section ... and
-- (d) no person to whom this paragraph applies shall be liable for any such damage or cost unless it resulted from anything done or
-- omitted to be done by the person either with intent to cause any such damage or cost or recklessly and in the knowledge that any
-- such damage or cost would probably result." (2): (a) servants or agents of the owner; (b) anyone "employed or engaged in any
-- capacity on board the ship or to perform any service for the ship"; (c) "any charterer of the ship (however described and including
-- a bareboat charterer), and any manager or operator"; (d) salvors "with the consent of the owner ... or on the instructions of a
-- competent public authority"; (e) anyone taking preventive measures; (f) servants or agents of (c), (d) or (e).
--
-- A person outside the list is not shielded: the Act then says nothing about that person's liability, which is left to the general
-- law (an inference; the text only withholds the shield).
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the master of the polluting ship`
    `a bareboat charterer`
    `the ship manager`
    `a salvor acting with the owner's consent`
    `a salvor acting on its own initiative`
    `a clean-up contractor`
    `the owner of the oil cargo`
    `the owner of another ship in the collision`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is within section 5(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a salvor acting on its own initiative` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the owner of the oil cargo` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the owner of another ship in the collision` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `acted intentionally or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is shielded by section 5` IF
    `the person is within section 5(2)` `the person` AND (NOT `acted intentionally or recklessly`)

§§ `5(3) -- environmental loss`

-- s 5(3): "The liability of the owner ... for any impairment of the environment is taken to be a liability ONLY in respect of -- (a)
-- any resulting loss of profits; and (b) the cost of any reasonable measures of reinstatement actually taken or to be taken." s 3(1):
-- the owner is liable for damage by contamination, the cost of measures "reasonably taken" to prevent or reduce it, and damage
-- caused by those measures.
DECLARE Loss IS ONE OF
    `contamination damage to a hotel's beachfront`
    `the cost of a reasonable clean-up`
    `a fish farm's lost profits from the contaminated water`
    `the cost of reasonable reinstatement of a mangrove`
    `the abstract value of the harm to the marine environment`

GIVEN `the loss` IS A Loss
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the loss is recoverable from the owner` IF
    CONSIDER `the loss`
    WHEN `the abstract value of the harm to the marine environment` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `6 and 15(3) -- limitation of liability`

-- s 6(2): "the relevant amount" is "(a) in relation to a ship not exceeding 5,000 tons -- 4.51 million special drawing rights; and (b)
-- in relation to a ship exceeding 5,000 tons -- 4.51 million special drawing rights together with an additional 631 special drawing
-- rights for each ton of its tonnage in excess of 5,000 tons up to a maximum amount of 89.77 million special drawing rights."
-- [S 486/2003]. (5): tonnage is gross tonnage under the 1969 Tonnage Convention. Converting to Singapore dollars (s 7(3)) is not
-- modelled.
GIVEN `tonnage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the owner's limit in SDR` MEANS
    IF `tonnage` AT MOST 5000 THEN 4510000
    ELSE IF 4510000 PLUS 631 TIMES (`tonnage` MINUS 5000) GREATER THAN 89770000 THEN 89770000
         ELSE 4510000 PLUS 631 TIMES (`tonnage` MINUS 5000)

-- s 6(4): the right to limit does not apply where it is proved the discharge or threat "resulted from anything done or omitted to be
-- done by the owner either with intent to cause any such damage or cost ... or recklessly and in the knowledge that any such damage or
-- cost would probably result." s 15(3): the insurer "may limit the insurer's liability ... in like manner and to the same extent as
-- the owner ... whether or not" the owner's conduct was of that kind.
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `the owner`
    `the insurer`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant, `the owner acted intentionally or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant may limit liability` IF
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `the insurer` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOT `the owner acted intentionally or recklessly`

§§ `12 -- time bar against the owner`

-- s 12: no action to enforce a claim under s 3 unless commenced "(a) not later than 3 years after the claim arose; and (b) not later
-- than 6 years after the occurrence, or first of the occurrences".
GIVEN `years from the claim arising` IS A NUMBER, `years from the occurrence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action against the owner is in time` IF
    `years from the claim arising` AT MOST 3 AND `years from the occurrence` AT MOST 6

§ `Compulsory insurance`

§§ `13(1), (2) and 18 -- when a certificate is required`

-- s 13(1): "Subsection (2) applies to any ship carrying in bulk as cargo MORE THAN 2,000 tons of oil." (2): the ship "must not enter or
-- leave any port in Singapore or enter or leave any offshore terminal in the territorial sea of Singapore and must not, if it is a
-- Singapore ship, enter or leave any port in any other country or any offshore terminal in the territorial sea of any other country,
-- unless there is in force a certificate" of insurance or other security satisfying Article VII of the Liability Convention.
-- s 18(2): for a State-owned ship in commercial use, a certificate issued by that State suffices (not modelled separately).
DECLARE Movement IS ONE OF
    `entering or leaving a Singapore port`
    `entering or leaving a Singapore offshore terminal`
    `entering or leaving a foreign port`
    `passing through Singapore waters without calling`

GIVEN `the ship` IS A Ship, `the movement` IS A Movement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certificate is required for the movement` IF
        (NOT `the ship`'s `a warship or government non-commercial ship`)
    AND `the ship`'s `tons of oil carried in bulk as cargo` GREATER THAN 2000
    AND CONSIDER `the movement`
        WHEN `entering or leaving a Singapore port` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `entering or leaving a Singapore offshore terminal` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `entering or leaving a foreign port` THEN `the ship`'s `a Singapore ship`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `13(3) -- who may issue the certificate`

-- s 13(3): "(a) if the ship is a Singapore ship -- a certificate issued by the Director; (b) if the ship is registered in a Liability
-- Convention country other than Singapore -- a certificate issued by or under the authority of the government of that other Liability
-- Convention country; and (c) if the ship is registered in a country which is not a Liability Convention country -- a certificate
-- issued by the Director or by or under the authority of the government of any Liability Convention country other than Singapore."
-- Regulations under s 13(4) recognising other certificates are not modelled.
DECLARE Registry IS ONE OF
    `Singapore`
    `another Liability Convention country`
    `a non-Convention country`

DECLARE Issuer IS ONE OF
    `the Singapore Director`
    `the government of the flag country`
    `the government of a third Liability Convention country`

GIVEN `the registry` IS A Registry, `the issuer` IS AN Issuer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate satisfies section 13(3)` IF
    CONSIDER `the registry`
    WHEN `Singapore` THEN
        CONSIDER `the issuer`
        WHEN `the Singapore Director` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `another Liability Convention country` THEN
        CONSIDER `the issuer`
        WHEN `the government of the flag country` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the issuer`
        WHEN `the government of the flag country` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `13(6), (7) and 20(2) -- offences`

-- s 13(6): entering or leaving in contravention of (2) -- "the master or the owner ... a fine not exceeding $1 million". (7): failing
-- to carry or produce the certificate -- the master, "a fine not exceeding $20,000". s 20(2): a detained ship proceeding to sea before
-- release -- the master, and the owner and anyone sending it to sea if party or privy, "a fine not exceeding $50,000 or ...
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or ... both". s 26(5): refusing or wilfully neglecting a Director's information
-- notice, or a knowingly or recklessly false statement -- $20,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `trading without an insurance certificate`
    `failing to carry or produce the certificate`
    `a detained ship going to sea`
    `failing to answer an information notice`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `trading without an insurance certificate` THEN 1000000
    WHEN `failing to carry or produce the certificate` THEN 20000
    WHEN `a detained ship going to sea` THEN 50000
    WHEN `failing to answer an information notice` THEN 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a detained ship going to sea` THEN 24
    WHEN `failing to answer an information notice` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

§ `The International Fund`

§§ `25(5), (6) -- who contributes`

-- s 25(4): the importer or receiver of oil carried by sea pays. (5): no liability "if the oil so imported or received in the year does
-- not exceed 150,000 tonnes." (6): "all the members of a group of companies are treated as a single person".
GIVEN `tonnes received by the company in the year` IS A NUMBER, `tonnes received by the rest of its group in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company must contribute to the Fund` IF
    `tonnes received by the company in the year` PLUS `tonnes received by the rest of its group in the year` GREATER THAN 150000

§§ `27(1), (6) -- when the Fund pays`

-- s 27(1): the Fund is liable for pollution damage in Singapore "if the person suffering the damage has been unable to obtain full
-- compensation under section 3 -- (a) because" the owner had the s 4(a) natural phenomenon, s 4(b) or s 4(c) defence; "(b) because the
-- owner or insurer liable for the damage cannot meet the owner's or insurer's obligations in full; or (c) because the damage exceeds
-- the liability under section 3 as limited". s 27(1)(a) does NOT list act of war, and (6)(a)(i): the Fund "incurs no obligation" if it
-- proves the damage "resulted from an act of war, hostilities, civil war or insurrection", or (ii) came from a warship or government
-- non-commercial ship, or (b) "the claimant cannot prove that the damage resulted from an occurrence involving a ship identified by
-- the claimant".
DECLARE Shortfall IS ONE OF
    `none -- the owner paid in full`
    `owner not liable -- act of war`
    `owner not liable -- natural phenomenon`
    `owner not liable -- outsider's sabotage`
    `owner not liable -- navigational aid failure`
    `owner and insurer cannot pay in full`
    `damage exceeds the owner's limit`

GIVEN `the shortfall` IS A Shortfall, `the claimant identified the ship` IS A BOOLEAN, `oil from a warship or government non-commercial ship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fund must compensate` IF
        `the claimant identified the ship`
    AND (NOT `oil from a warship or government non-commercial ship`)
    AND CONSIDER `the shortfall`
        WHEN `none -- the owner paid in full` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `owner not liable -- act of war` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `27(7), (9) -- the claimant's own fault`

-- s 27(7): if the damage resulted wholly or partly from the claimant's intent or negligence, the Fund "may ... be exonerated wholly or
-- partly". (9): that "do[es] not apply where the pollution damage consists of the costs of preventive measures or any damage caused by
-- such measures."
GIVEN `the claimant was at fault` IS A BOOLEAN, `the claim is for preventive measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fund may be exonerated for the claimant's fault` IF
    `the claimant was at fault` AND (NOT `the claim is for preventive measures`)

§§ `28(1) -- the Fund's cap`

-- s 28(1)(a): "the total sum of that amount and the amount of compensation actually paid under section 3 ... shall not exceed 203
-- million special drawing rights"; (b) for "an exceptional, inevitable and irresistible natural phenomenon" the Fund's compensation
-- "shall not exceed 135 million special drawing rights"; (c) the maximum in (a) and (b) "shall be 300.74 million" where 3 Fund
-- Convention countries together received at least 600 million tons in the preceding calendar year. [S 486/2003]
-- Read literally, (a) caps the Fund and the owner together, (b) caps the Fund alone; the natural-phenomenon cap is LOWER than the
-- general one. In a natural-phenomenon case the owner pays nothing under s 3 anyway (s 4(a)).
GIVEN `a natural phenomenon` IS A BOOLEAN, `the 600 million ton condition holds` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid under section 3` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Fund's maximum in SDR` MEANS
    IF `the 600 million ton condition holds` AND `a natural phenomenon` THEN 300740000
    ELSE IF `a natural phenomenon` THEN 135000000
         ELSE IF `the 600 million ton condition holds` THEN `what remains of` 300740000 `paid under section 3`
              ELSE `what remains of` 203000000 `paid under section 3`

GIVEN `cap` IS A NUMBER, `paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what remains of` MEANS
    IF `paid` GREATER THAN `cap` THEN 0 ELSE `cap` MINUS `paid`

§§ `28(2) and 7(2)(b) -- pro-rata sharing`

-- s 28(2): where established claims exceed the amount available, it is distributed so that "the proportion between any established
-- claim and the amount of compensation actually recovered ... is the same for all claimants." s 7(2)(b) distributes the owner's
-- limitation fund "in proportion to their claims" in the same way.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A NUMBER, `all established claims` IS A NUMBER, `the amount available` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the claimant's share` MEANS
    IF `all established claims` AT MOST `the amount available` THEN `the claim`
    ELSE `the claim` TIMES `the amount available` DIVIDED BY `all established claims`

§§ `30 -- time bar against the Fund`

-- s 30(1): an action against the Fund must be commenced, or a third party notice of an action against the owner or insurer given to
-- the Fund, "not later than 3 years after the claim against the Fund arose". (3): and in any case the action must be commenced "not
-- later than 6 years after the occurrence, or first of the occurrences".
GIVEN `years from the Fund claim arising` IS A NUMBER, `the Fund was given notice within 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN, `years from the incident` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action against the Fund is in time` IF
        (`years from the Fund claim arising` AT MOST 3 OR `the Fund was given notice within 3 years`)
    AND `years from the incident` AT MOST 6
